{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== HANDOFF #10 ADDENDUM — written later in the same session; supersedes #10's board. ===\n\n**e369 IS NOW 24/26 CHILDREN CLOSED.** Only two remain:\n  * 5200 (J11) — in_progress. Harness run 30724309686 (main @ 216ceb830) is in flight with change\n    1188's fixes. Read it, then triage the five genuine findings in the \"HARNESS RUN 3\" comment on\n    5200. Nothing else blocks that ticket.\n  * cc77 — in_progress, claimed, DELIBERATELY NOT IMPLEMENTED. See the blocking discovery below.\n\nCLOSED THIS SESSION (7): f2f3 (S1), 9f0b, fe15, 6758 (S2), b586, 6a91 — plus the epic's headline\nstaying proven throughout.\nMERGED THIS SESSION (9): 1177, 1179, 1182, 1183, 1185, 1186, 1188, 1190, 1191.\n\n*** cc77 — DO NOT IMPLEMENT THE PLAN AS WRITTEN. ITS PREMISE IS FALSE AGAINST CURRENT CODE. ***\nFull evidence is on the ticket. The short version: the plan says annotating a param as\n`TicketTransport` makes mypy reject a call to an undeclared member. It does NOT.\n`class TicketTransport(Protocol, metaclass=_TransportPortMeta)` — J9's metaclass, carrying a\n`# type: ignore[misc]` — makes mypy stop attribute-checking the annotated type entirely. Isolated\nwith a controlled two-function probe: an identical call through a PLAIN `Protocol` errors\n`[attr-defined]`; through `TicketTransport` it does not. Implementing the plan would ship ~20\nannotations that look rigorous and enforce nothing — the exact failure the ticket was written to\nprevent, arriving by a route it did not anticipate, and invisible in review because\n`make typecheck` would stay green having never been going to say anything.\nThe metaclass is load-bearing for J9's RUNTIME guard (it defeats `ABCMeta`'s isinstance cache, so a\nclass that once conformed cannot keep reporting True after losing a member). So cc77 must first\ndecide: (a) give mypy a checkable view while keeping the runtime guard — declare the Protocol\nplainly and attach the uncached-isinstance behaviour to a separate subclass or function; or\n(b) accept static blindness, rely on the runtime guard, and retire the premise (the annotations\nwould still be worth doing for readability and Serena/Pyright navigation, bug dbf9, but NOT as\nenforcement). Either way the plan needs rewriting before code is written.\n\n--- TWO ENVIRONMENT TRAPS THAT COST ME TIME; BOTH ARE AVOIDABLE ---\n 1. **NEVER USE `FETCH_HEAD` WHILE A BACKGROUND JOB IS FETCHING.** `FETCH_HEAD` is one file per\n    repo. A background mirror-poll loop doing `git fetch origin` clobbered it between my fetch and\n    my checkout, so `git checkout -B x FETCH_HEAD` landed on an unrelated commit (\"Update\n    README.md\", ADRs only to 0031). The close gate then correctly reported that `_backend.py` and\n    both ADRs \"do not exist\" — which reads alarmingly like the work vanished. **Check out an\n    EXPLICIT SHA.**\n 2. **`rebar` IS AN EDITABLE INSTALL FROM THIS CHECKOUT, so parking the worktree on an older\n    commit DOWNGRADES THE TOOL.** A `review-plan` crashed with\n    `CriteriaError: cannot load criterion prompt for 'G7'` purely because HEAD sat on a commit\n    predating `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_G7.md`. It is not a plan defect and not a\n    registry drift — re-run from current main. Corollary: run LLM gates with the worktree ON\n    CURRENT MAIN, which is also what the attestation wants.\n\n--- ONE MORE GATE BEHAVIOUR WORTH KNOWING ---\nA PARENT's close can fail with `stale-pin-drift` because a CHILD's plan changed after the parent\nwas reviewed (b586 hit this once S2's plan was rewritten). The remedy is exactly what the error\nsays: re-run `rebar review-plan <parent>` and retry the close. This is the same \"a review pins its\ndependencies' material\" rule AGENTS.md states for reviewing in dependency order — it applies to\ncloses too, not just claims."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785629943570230001,"uuid":"d42ad283-4afd-4915-a686-0ab3f764d0d1"}